    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Benthic Survey\"\nmenutitle: \"Benthic Survey\"\n---\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\nThe deep-sea benthos is remote and much harder to reach than shallower, coastal seafloor. We mainly uses four gears to collect our data:\n\n## Epibenthic Sledge (EBS)\n\nAs the name suggests, EBS is similar to a trawl on the seafloor. It is optimized to capture the epifauna and infauna of the first few centimeters. \n\nOf course, EBS leaves a trawling trail behind it and the gear itself is also sensitive to boulders on the seafloor. Therefore the EBS is only deployed at soft sediment plains and the trawling distances are normally planned between 50 to 100 meters. \n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-ebs\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EBS lifted by the winch and about to be deployed.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/ebs_deploy.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;EBS lifted by the winch and about to be deployed.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Stefanie Kaiser (left) and Katharina Kohlenbach (right) monitoring the tension meter of the which. It is the primary way to see whether EBS is trawling smoothly on the seafloor.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/ebs_tensionmeter.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Stefanie Kaiser (left) and Katharina Kohlenbach (right) monitoring the tension meter of the which. It is the primary way to see whether EBS is trawling smoothly on the seafloor.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;An official certificate for participating the cruise.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/ebs_sticker.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;An official certificate for participating the cruise.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The collected samples are washed directly on the deck. &quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/decksort3.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;The collected samples are washed directly on the deck.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Saskia Brix (left, first) already sorting out some specimens.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/decksort1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Saskia Brix (left, first) already sorting out some specimens.&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/ebs_deploy.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\">EBS lifted by the winch and about to be deployed.</div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## Grabs\n\nCompared to EBS, different grabs are used, also at the area where EBS is impossible to sample due to dense boulders on the seafloor. Among all of them, the Box Corer is one of the most used gear, which always brings the exact area of sediment back onboard, while keeping the sediment surface and internal structure intact. Allowing us to conduct more detailed quantitative analysis. \n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-grabs\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Box Corer is back onboard and covered by deep-sea mud.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_recover.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Box Corer is back onboard and covered by deep-sea mud.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Sometimes the box corer just got to the right place, and the epifauna comes on deck intact.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_photo.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Sometimes the box corer just got to the right place, and the epifauna comes on deck intact.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The sediments of the box corer are separated by depth layer and homogenised before going through sieves.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_wash.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;The sediments of the box corer are separated by depth layer and homogenised before going through sieves.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;You may say homogenising mud is an overcomplication - it&#39;s not as simple as playing with mud. It actually does require skills.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_wash3.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;You may say homogenising mud is an overcomplication - it&#39;s not as simple as playing with mud. It actually does require skills.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Washing samples might sound easy, but it usually requires many more people ... including two people with cameras.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_wash2.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Washing samples might sound easy, but it usually requires many more people ... including two people with cameras.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;All of our gears have names. Here are Kalli the box corer (left), and Ursula the EBS (right).&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/bc_ebs.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;All of our gears have names. Here are Kalli the box corer (left), and Ursula the EBS (right).&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/bc_recover.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\">Box Corer is back onboard and covered by deep-sea mud.</div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## Remotely Operated Vehicle (ROV)\n\nThe ROV is becoming a star in the deep-sea exploration. Of course we would like to work with them. _ROV Phoca_ from GEOMAR is a very special member of us, who will bring our Benthic Lander Observatory System onto the seafloor. And if it's not busy deploying landers, we also love to have some deep-sea \"Spaziergang\" with astonishing 4K cameras and our sampling boxes. \n\nDifferent from EBS and grabs, as the videos of the ROV are transmitted real-time to the vessel, we can see what's down there and sample very specifically, leaving minimal disturbance on the seafloor.\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-rov\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;_ROV Phoca_ ready to splash and dive&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_deployment.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&lt;em&gt;ROV Phoca&lt;\\/em&gt; ready to splash and dive&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Videos are shown in real-time for precise coordination between ROV pilots, bridges, and scientists.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_deckstation.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Videos are shown in real-time for precise coordination between ROV pilots, bridges, and scientists.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Visuals are plugged into the ship intranet and are shown on bigger screens for scientists.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_showroom2.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Visuals are plugged into the ship intranet and are shown on bigger screens for scientists.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;It needs at least three scientists for each ROV dive: a dive lead making decisions, a protocol write documenting everything we see and do, and an emotional supporter also responsible to provide coffee. But normally we have way more people in the science room.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_showroom1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;It needs at least three scientists for each ROV dive: a dive lead making decisions, a protocol write documenting everything we see and do, and an emotional supporter also responsible to provide coffee. But normally we have way more people in the science room.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;When people are off-shift, they also love watching what&#39;s going on under there.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_showroom.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;When people are off-shift, they also love watching what&#39;s going on under there.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Two pilots are manipulating the ROV at all time. They sit in a separate ROV container, which allows them to focus on flying the ROV completely.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_container1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Two pilots are manipulating the ROV at all time. They sit in a separate ROV container, which allows them to focus on flying the ROV completely.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Samples are taken by one of the pilot manipulating the robotic arms.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_container2.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Samples are taken by one of the pilot manipulating the robotic arms.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;We the manipulator, we can see before our samples, therefore only collecting those we really need.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/row_sample2.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;We the manipulator, we can see before our samples, therefore only collecting those we really need.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Even the rest-over in the containers are precious samples for us.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/rov_sample1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Even the rest-over in the containers are precious samples for us.&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/rov_deployment.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\"><em>ROV Phoca</em> ready to splash and dive</div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## Ocean Floor Observation System (OFOS)\n\nSimilar to ROV, OFOS is another gear based on imagery data collection. However, OFOS is for observation only - it has no manipulators, nor can it sample the seafloor. Also without any thruster, OFOS completely relied on the vessel towing it, but therefore, it's much easier to deploy. \n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<figure id=\"roulette-ofos\" class=\"roulette-container\" style=\"margin: 0; padding: 0;\" data-images=\"[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;OFOS lifted and about to be deployed.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/ofos_deploy.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;OFOS lifted and about to be deployed.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;During the OFOS dive, a winch operator controls the distance from OFOS to the seafloor, our Postdoc, Lili, takes pictures and documents what&#39;s on the seafloor.&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/ofos_room1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;During the OFOS dive, a winch operator controls the distance from OFOS to the seafloor, our Postdoc, Lili, takes pictures and documents what&#39;s on the seafloor.&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Within no time, a crowd of the crews will assemble in the hanger ...&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/hanger1.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Within no time, a crowd of the crews will assemble in the hanger ...&quot;},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;... to watch the seafloor&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;../../assets/img/hanger2.webp&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;... to watch the seafloor&quot;}]\">\n<div class=\"roulette-stage\" style=\"height: 400px; position: relative; width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; overflow: hidden; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div>\n<a href=\"../../assets/img/ofos_deploy.webp\" class=\"lightbox\" style=\"display: none;\">dummy</a>\n<div class=\"roulette-thumbnails\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"r-track\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption class=\"roulette-caption\" style=\"text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n<div class=\"caption-text\" style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0 auto;\">OFOS lifted and about to be deployed.</div>\n</figcaption>\n</figure>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n<hr>\n\n[&#8592; Back](../../index.qmd){.btn .btn-outline-primary role='button'}\n",
